          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A Tale of Three Intersecting Lines"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.122,
            0.662,
            0.145
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "How do we construct this triangle more efficiently?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.153,
            0.848,
            0.21
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Choose one of the given lengths to be the base of the triangle: say 4 cm. Draw the base. Let A and B be the base vertices, and call the third vertex C. Let "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { A C } = 5"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " cm and BC = 6 cm."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.259,
            0.849,
            0.334
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Like we did in the case of equilateral triangles, let us first get all the points that are at a 5 cm distance from A. These points lie on the circle whose centre is A and has radius 5 cm. The point C must lie somewhere on this circle. How do we find it?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.349,
            0.339,
            0.65,
            0.582
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 6,
              "bbox": [
                0.349,
                0.339,
                0.65,
                0.582
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_3_image_6.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.586,
            0.825,
            0.625
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We will make use of the fact that the point C is 6 cm away from B. Construct an arc of radius 6 cm from B."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.21,
            0.628,
